          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part I"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.108,
            0.491,
            0.321
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.123,
                0.108,
                0.491,
                0.321
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_10_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.501,
            0.109,
            0.878,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here, we have two congruent circles centered at A and B. Each one passes through the centre of the other one. The circles intersect at C and D. We need to find the total length of the two red arcs shown here, in terms of the radius r unit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.502,
            0.243,
            0.877,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider the triangle with vertices A, B, C. Since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { A B } = r ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "AC = r, BC = r,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the triangle is equilateral, hence "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle CAB = 60^{\\circ} ="
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { C B A }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.36,
            0.828,
            0.381
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Similarly "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle BAD = 60^{\\circ} = \\angle ABD"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . It follows that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle CAD = 120^{\\circ} = \\angle CBD."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.391,
            0.883,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence, each dotted arc is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the circumference of the circle on which it lies. Hence, the total length of the two red arcs is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\times \\frac{2}{3} \\times 2\\pi r = \\frac{8}{3}\\pi r"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.479,
            0.475,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.137,
                0.479,
                0.475,
                0.654
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_10_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.26,
                0.656,
                0.339,
                0.672
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 6.13"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.482,
            0.482,
            0.877,
            0.697
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In Fig. 6.13, we see points P and Q and two paths connecting them. The first path is made up of the semicircle a. The other path is made up of three semicircles (b, c and d). Which path is longer? Choose one: (i) Path a is longer. (ii) Path "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b \\; + \\; c \\; + \\; d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is longer. (iii) The two paths have equal length. (Try to answer this before reading on.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.718,
            0.886,
            0.829
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us solve the problem using algebra. Let the radii of the semicircles "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a , b , c ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " d be denoted by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\bar { a ^ { \\prime } } , \\bar { b ^ { \\prime } } , \\bar { c ^ { \\prime } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "d ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Then the length of semicircle "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a \\mathrm{i}s \\frac{1}{2} (2\\pi) a' = \\pi a'."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Similarly, the lengths of the semicircles "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b , \\; c ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and d are "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\pi b ^ { \\prime } ,   \\pi c ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and πd'. So, the length of the second path is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\pi ( b ^ { \\prime } + c ^ { \\prime } + d ^ { \\prime } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and that of the first path is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\pi a ^ { \\prime } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.829,
            0.886,
            0.909
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Which is bigger, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b' + c' + d'"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a ^ { \\prime } \\nmid"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Do you see that neither one is bigger? They are equal! Because, the length of PQ is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 a ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and it is also equal to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2b' + 2c' + 2d'"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . It follows that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a^{\\prime} = b^{\\prime} + c^{\\prime} + d^{\\prime}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Hence, the two paths have equal length!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
